ifa/issues/112 -- NONDET: the same source emits two different .c files across identical compiles. Both are semantically correct; they differ only in WHICH of two equivalent CreationSets becomes the struct representative (_CG_ps12229 vs _CG_ps12231) and hence in Sym id assignment. Exposed (not caused) by issues/121's canonical field promotion: once two sibling subclasses stop getting different field ORDERS they become genuinely equivalent, and ifa/112's pointer-hashed tiebreak starts deciding between them. Flips to PASS when 112 lands.
